From a3d7bc1cfad176138cf9b9b31b8335aa9718af9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Velle Sinclair <brncomputerhelp@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 08:10:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 51/53] fix(filesystem): a virtual file reads whole every time
 it is opened

VirtualAdapter::open handed every caller the same stream, and the first
to read it left it at its end, so the next caller to open the file read
nothing. The files the engine adds itself were each read once per scene,
which hid it; every text layer with effects opens the same model (the
next commit), and all but the first failed to parse it.

Each open now gets a stream of its own over a copy of the bytes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TrYdVZ7ULsVD9WKX2Az4Mw
---
 CMakeLists.txt                                |  3 +-
 src/WallpaperEngine/Data/Utils/MemoryStream.h | 10 +++++
 .../FileSystem/Adapters/Virtual.cpp           |  4 +-
 .../Testing/Cases/VirtualFiles.cpp            | 45 +++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 60 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/WallpaperEngine/Testing/Cases/VirtualFiles.cpp

